    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    User / Transaction\n",
        "                           │\n",
        "                           ▼\n",
        "                      AI Agent\n",
        "                           │\n",
        "              ┌────────────┼────────────┐\n",
        "              ▼            ▼            ▼\n",
        "          Short-term   Long-term    Knowledge\n",
        "            State        Memory        Base\n",
        "              │            │            │\n",
        "              └────────────┼────────────┘\n",
        "                           ▼\n",
        "                    Context Builder\n",
        "                           │\n",
        "                           ▼\n",
        "                         LLM"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "U8Ycy4WMfYuX"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "| Type                  | Simple definition                                                       | Example                                                                          |\n",
        "| --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n",
        "| **Context Memory**    | Information available to the AI **right now** for the current response. | User says, “My name is Vimal.” → AI can use “Vimal” in the current conversation. |\n",
        "| **Short-Term Memory** | Information the AI keeps **during the current task/session**.           | Researcher finds data → Analyst uses that data later in the same workflow.       |\n",
        "| **Long-Term Memory**  | Information **stored for future conversations or tasks**.               | User says, “I prefer Python.” → System stores this preference and uses it later. |\n",
        "| **Knowledge Memory**  | External information the AI can **retrieve when needed**.               | AI retrieves information about AML rules from a company policy document.         |\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "wKRaKenAfnO6"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Types of Long-Term Memory\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Semantic Memory\n",
        "Definition: Stores facts and information that the AI can remember for future conversations.\n",
        "Example:\n",
        "\n",
        "\"My name is Vimal and I work at HSBC.\"\n",
        "\n",
        "2. Episodic Memory\n",
        "Definition: Stores past events or experiences from previous interactions.\n",
        "Example:\n",
        "\n",
        "\"Yesterday, Vimal asked me to explain LangChain memory.\"\n",
        "\n",
        "3. Procedural Memory\n",
        "Definition: Stores instructions or knowledge about how to perform a task.\n",
        "Example:\n",
        "\n",
        "\"When booking a flight, first ask for the destination, then the travel date.\""
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "_tVd3X_UokXG"
      }
